<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">shoot</ansi>

Fire a loaded ranged weapon at a target in your room or an
adjacent room.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">shoot <target></ansi>
      Fire at a target in the same room.

  <ansi fg="command">shoot <target> <direction></ansi>
      Fire into the adjacent room in that direction and strike
      a target there.

The weapon must be loaded before it can fire. Use
<ansi fg="command">reload</ansi> after each shot to ready it for the next one.
Reloading draws one round of ammunition from a matching bundle
in your pack (arrows for a bow, bolts for a crossbow, shot for
a sling or pistol). When a bundle runs dry you will be told it
was your last.

Each shot uses your combat round. Cross-room fire does not
automatically pull you into melee — the target must close the
distance to engage.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Progression ━━━</ansi>

Ranged-combat improves through use. Shots that connect have a
chance to advance the skill. Perception governs aimed-shot
accuracy and damage.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help reload</ansi>,
  <ansi fg="command">help ranged-combat</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help wield</ansi>
